<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $44.9 mln Sept 9.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $44.9 mln Sept 9.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $44.9 million surplus on September 9 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 9</p>
<p>Exports: $219.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $132.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $199.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $241.1 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $44.9 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.261 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $840 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $754 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.149 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $26 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
